        "composer": {
          "answer": "INC-204 began at 10:02 on July 21, when API CPU was elevated and latency rising; a memory leak was only an unconfirmed initial hypothesis (A009). By 10:17, retries had risen after the client-timeout rollout, and disabling automatic retries reduced CPU and queue depth as rollback began (A010). The postmortem concluded that the rollout caused retry amplification, with elevated CPU as a downstream symptom; heap analysis rejected the memory-leak hypothesis (A011). The addendum changed only the incident start time, correcting the earlier 10:00 entry to 10:02; it did not change the retry-amplification root-cause assessment (A012).",
